1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,993
Sweetheart, in December of two thousand twenty-one,

2
00:00:03,993 --> 00:00:06,733
my friend Helen walked into a fancy

3
00:00:06,733 --> 00:00:08,925
truck dealership in Florida,

4
00:00:08,925 --> 00:00:10,804
seventy-seven years old,

5
00:00:10,804 --> 00:00:12,762
in her gardening clothes,

6
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:15,580
carrying an old coffee can under her

7
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:15,894
arm.

8
00:00:16,074 --> 00:00:18,770
The top salesman looked her up and

9
00:00:18,770 --> 00:00:19,881
down and said,

10
00:00:19,881 --> 00:00:22,498
ma'am, the used lot is across the

11
00:00:22,498 --> 00:00:23,132
highway.

12
00:00:23,312 --> 00:00:24,624
Everybody laughed.

13
00:00:24,804 --> 00:00:27,221
He didn't know what was in that

14
00:00:27,221 --> 00:00:28,078
coffee can.

15
00:00:28,258 --> 00:00:30,476
Forty-six thousand dollars.

16
00:00:30,656 --> 00:00:31,643
Cash.

17
00:00:31,993 --> 00:00:34,181
Tonight I'm going to tell you who

18
00:00:34,181 --> 00:00:35,440
that money was for,

19
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:38,159
why Helen walked right past that salesman

20
00:00:38,159 --> 00:00:40,281
to the newest girl on the floor,

21
00:00:40,281 --> 00:00:42,469
and what happened to both of them

22
00:00:42,469 --> 00:00:43,928
by the end of the day.

23
00:00:44,108 --> 00:00:45,052
Stay with me,

24
00:00:45,052 --> 00:00:47,740
honey, because the look on that man's

25
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:50,792
face is something Helen still describes to

26
00:00:50,792 --> 00:00:53,117
me on the phone every Christmas.

27
00:00:53,467 --> 00:00:55,896
Helen and I grew up together in

28
00:00:55,896 --> 00:00:57,228
Mansfield, honey.

29
00:00:57,408 --> 00:01:00,224
She married a mechanic named Frank,

30
00:01:00,224 --> 00:01:03,202
the best mechanic in Richland County.

31
00:01:03,382 --> 00:01:06,087
He could fix anything with an engine.

32
00:01:06,267 --> 00:01:07,911
They never had much,

33
00:01:07,911 --> 00:01:09,227
but Frank saved.

34
00:01:09,407 --> 00:01:11,743
Every week, he put a few dollars

35
00:01:11,743 --> 00:01:13,787
into a red coffee can on the

36
00:01:13,787 --> 00:01:15,247
shelf in his garage.

37
00:01:15,427 --> 00:01:17,737
Every week for forty years.

38
00:01:17,917 --> 00:01:20,466
He never told anybody how much was

39
00:01:20,466 --> 00:01:22,341
in there, not even Helen.

40
00:01:22,691 --> 00:01:24,149
When Frank retired,

41
00:01:24,149 --> 00:01:26,528
they moved to a little house in

42
00:01:26,528 --> 00:01:28,294
Florida, near Sarasota,

43
00:01:28,294 --> 00:01:30,136
close to their daughter,

44
00:01:30,136 --> 00:01:33,514
because Helen's knees couldn't take the Ohio

45
00:01:33,514 --> 00:01:34,742
winters anymore.

46
00:01:34,922 --> 00:01:37,714
Frank passed in two thousand twenty,

47
00:01:37,714 --> 00:01:38,799
in the spring.

48
00:01:38,979 --> 00:01:41,786
And when Helen was going through his

49
00:01:41,786 --> 00:01:43,267
garage that summer,

50
00:01:43,267 --> 00:01:45,917
she took down that red coffee can,

51
00:01:45,917 --> 00:01:47,009
and opened it,

52
00:01:47,009 --> 00:01:49,893
and sat down on an overturned bucket.

53
00:01:50,073 --> 00:01:51,277
It was packed,

54
00:01:51,277 --> 00:01:54,287
honey, tight, with rolled-up bills.

55
00:01:54,467 --> 00:01:55,965
And a note on top.

56
00:01:56,315 --> 00:01:57,777
The note said,

57
00:01:57,777 --> 00:01:58,404
Helen.

58
00:01:58,584 --> 00:02:00,764
This is for Caleb's truck,

59
00:02:00,764 --> 00:02:02,358
when he comes home.

60
00:02:02,538 --> 00:02:04,623
Don't let anybody talk you out of

61
00:02:04,623 --> 00:02:04,813
it.

62
00:02:04,993 --> 00:02:06,723
Love, Frank.

63
00:02:06,903 --> 00:02:09,177
Caleb was their grandson,

64
00:02:09,177 --> 00:02:10,177
sweetheart.

65
00:02:10,357 --> 00:02:11,646
Frank's shadow.

66
00:02:11,826 --> 00:02:14,505
That boy had been in Frank's garage

67
00:02:14,505 --> 00:02:15,884
since he was four,

68
00:02:15,884 --> 00:02:17,491
handing him wrenches.

69
00:02:17,671 --> 00:02:19,493
And when he was eighteen,

70
00:02:19,493 --> 00:02:21,096
he joined the Marines.

71
00:02:21,276 --> 00:02:24,048
He was in Japan when his grandpa

72
00:02:24,048 --> 00:02:24,481
died.

73
00:02:24,661 --> 00:02:27,052
He couldn't come home for the funeral.

74
00:02:27,232 --> 00:02:29,176
In a minute I'll tell you why

75
00:02:29,176 --> 00:02:31,052
that truck mattered so much.

76
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:33,123
When Caleb was twelve,

77
00:02:33,123 --> 00:02:35,549
honey, he and Frank used to sit

78
00:02:35,549 --> 00:02:38,523
on the tailgate of Frank's old pickup,

79
00:02:38,523 --> 00:02:42,123
eating sunflower seeds and watching the trucks

80
00:02:42,123 --> 00:02:43,766
go by on the highway.

81
00:02:43,946 --> 00:02:46,759
And Caleb would point at the new

82
00:02:46,759 --> 00:02:48,957
ones, the big shiny ones,

83
00:02:48,957 --> 00:02:50,451
and say, Grandpa,

84
00:02:50,451 --> 00:02:53,264
someday I'm going to have one of

85
00:02:53,264 --> 00:02:53,791
those.

86
00:02:53,971 --> 00:02:55,414
And Frank would say,

87
00:02:55,414 --> 00:02:58,082
when you come home from wherever life

88
00:02:58,082 --> 00:03:00,101
takes you, I'll buy you one.

89
00:03:00,281 --> 00:03:01,744
That's a promise.

90
00:03:02,095 --> 00:03:04,752
Caleb was coming home on leave the

91
00:03:04,752 --> 00:03:06,471
week before Christmas,

92
00:03:06,471 --> 00:03:09,911
twenty twenty-one, his first time home since

93
00:03:09,911 --> 00:03:10,848
the funeral.

94
00:03:11,028 --> 00:03:13,533
And Helen was going to keep Frank's

95
00:03:13,533 --> 00:03:14,105
promise.

96
00:03:14,285 --> 00:03:16,669
She counted the money at the kitchen

97
00:03:16,669 --> 00:03:17,861
table three times.

98
00:03:18,041 --> 00:03:21,315
Forty-six thousand, two hundred dollars.

99
00:03:21,495 --> 00:03:23,422
And on December fifteenth,

100
00:03:23,422 --> 00:03:25,422
she put the coffee can in a

101
00:03:25,422 --> 00:03:27,942
grocery bag, got in her old Buick,

102
00:03:27,942 --> 00:03:30,980
and drove to the biggest truck dealership

103
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:31,572
in town.

104
00:03:31,922 --> 00:03:34,879
Helen called me the night before,

105
00:03:34,879 --> 00:03:35,417
honey.

106
00:03:35,597 --> 00:03:37,205
She said, Ruth,

107
00:03:37,205 --> 00:03:38,383
I'm scared.

108
00:03:38,563 --> 00:03:40,712
I've never bought a car in my

109
00:03:40,712 --> 00:03:41,083
life.

110
00:03:41,263 --> 00:03:42,842
Frank did all that.

111
00:03:43,022 --> 00:03:44,543
What if they cheat me?

112
00:03:44,723 --> 00:03:45,575
And I said,

113
00:03:45,575 --> 00:03:48,906
Helen, you raised three children and buried

114
00:03:48,906 --> 00:03:49,680
a husband.

115
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:51,323
You can buy a truck.

116
00:03:51,503 --> 00:03:54,324
Just remember what Frank always said.

117
00:03:54,504 --> 00:03:56,707
The one who listens is the one

118
00:03:56,707 --> 00:03:57,662
you buy from.

119
00:03:57,842 --> 00:04:00,164
She didn't know yet how right he

120
00:04:00,164 --> 00:04:00,454
was.

121
00:04:00,634 --> 00:04:02,911
I'll tell you how she found out

122
00:04:02,911 --> 00:04:03,792
in a minute.

123
00:04:04,142 --> 00:04:06,401
She barely slept that night,

124
00:04:06,401 --> 00:04:07,289
sweetheart.

125
00:04:07,469 --> 00:04:09,607
She kept getting up to check that

126
00:04:09,607 --> 00:04:11,616
the coffee can was still in the

127
00:04:11,616 --> 00:04:14,272
kitchen cabinet, behind the cereal boxes.

128
00:04:14,452 --> 00:04:16,191
At three in the morning,

129
00:04:16,191 --> 00:04:18,582
she sat at the table with Frank's

130
00:04:18,582 --> 00:04:20,032
photograph and said,

131
00:04:20,032 --> 00:04:21,191
out loud, Frank,

132
00:04:21,191 --> 00:04:22,568
I'm going to do it.

133
00:04:22,748 --> 00:04:24,826
I'm going to keep your promise.

134
00:04:25,006 --> 00:04:27,150
And she told me she could have

135
00:04:27,150 --> 00:04:30,080
sworn she smelled motor oil and sunflower

136
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:31,867
seeds, just for a second.

137
00:04:32,218 --> 00:04:35,084
If you're enjoying Grandma's story,

138
00:04:35,084 --> 00:04:37,296
tap the like button for me,

139
00:04:37,296 --> 00:04:38,197
sweetheart.

140
00:04:38,377 --> 00:04:41,593
It helps more people find these stories.

141
00:04:41,773 --> 00:04:44,133
Helen had been out in her garden

142
00:04:44,133 --> 00:04:45,535
all morning, honey,

143
00:04:45,535 --> 00:04:47,821
and she didn't think to change.

144
00:04:48,001 --> 00:04:50,877
Old canvas pants with dirt on the

145
00:04:50,877 --> 00:04:52,882
knees, a faded sun hat,

146
00:04:52,882 --> 00:04:55,234
and Frank's old work shirt.

147
00:04:55,414 --> 00:04:57,565
She walked into that showroom,

148
00:04:57,565 --> 00:04:59,931
all glass and chrome and cold air

149
00:04:59,931 --> 00:05:02,583
conditioning, and she stood next to a

150
00:05:02,583 --> 00:05:05,235
big red truck and waited for somebody

151
00:05:05,235 --> 00:05:06,096
to help her.

152
00:05:06,445 --> 00:05:09,163
There were four salesmen at the desks,

153
00:05:09,163 --> 00:05:09,592
honey.

154
00:05:09,772 --> 00:05:11,060
They all looked up.

155
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:13,284
They all looked back down.

156
00:05:13,464 --> 00:05:15,171
She waited ten minutes.

157
00:05:15,351 --> 00:05:18,193
Then one of them finally walked over,

158
00:05:18,193 --> 00:05:20,883
a man about forty with slicked hair

159
00:05:20,883 --> 00:05:22,189
and a gold watch.

160
00:05:22,369 --> 00:05:24,958
His name tag said Brad.

161
00:05:25,138 --> 00:05:27,729
And before Helen could say a word,

162
00:05:27,729 --> 00:05:28,872
he said, ma'am,

163
00:05:28,872 --> 00:05:31,540
if you're looking for the restroom,

164
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:32,835
it's in the back.

165
00:05:33,015 --> 00:05:35,522
And if you're looking for something in

166
00:05:35,522 --> 00:05:37,831
your budget, the used lot is across

167
00:05:37,831 --> 00:05:38,623
the highway.

168
00:05:38,972 --> 00:05:41,500
And the other salesmen laughed,

169
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:42,397
sweetheart.

170
00:05:42,577 --> 00:05:45,171
Helen said her face went hot as

171
00:05:45,171 --> 00:05:45,840
a stove.

172
00:05:46,020 --> 00:05:48,655
She said, I'm looking at this truck.

173
00:05:48,835 --> 00:05:50,025
And Brad said,

174
00:05:50,025 --> 00:05:52,575
that one's sixty-two thousand,

175
00:05:52,575 --> 00:05:53,085
ma'am.

176
00:05:53,265 --> 00:05:55,786
And he looked at her grocery bag,

177
00:05:55,786 --> 00:05:56,855
and he smiled,

178
00:05:56,855 --> 00:05:57,772
and he said,

179
00:05:57,772 --> 00:05:59,453
we don't take coupons.

180
00:05:59,633 --> 00:06:01,361
And he walked away,

181
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:02,907
back to his desk,

182
00:06:02,907 --> 00:06:05,089
and picked up his phone.

183
00:06:05,269 --> 00:06:07,443
In a minute I'll tell you who

184
00:06:07,443 --> 00:06:08,567
came over next.

185
00:06:08,916 --> 00:06:11,269
A young woman came over from the

186
00:06:11,269 --> 00:06:12,666
back corner, honey.

187
00:06:12,846 --> 00:06:16,230
About twenty-six, in a black blazer that

188
00:06:16,230 --> 00:06:17,668
didn't quite fit,

189
00:06:17,668 --> 00:06:20,375
with a name tag that said Maria,

190
00:06:20,375 --> 00:06:21,474
and under it,

191
00:06:21,474 --> 00:06:22,912
in small letters,

192
00:06:22,912 --> 00:06:24,097
sales trainee.

193
00:06:24,277 --> 00:06:26,730
She'd been sitting at the desk nobody

194
00:06:26,730 --> 00:06:28,654
wanted, by the bathroom door.

195
00:06:28,834 --> 00:06:30,400
She said, ma'am,

196
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,456
I'm sorry about that.

197
00:06:32,636 --> 00:06:34,475
Can I get you a glass of

198
00:06:34,475 --> 00:06:34,935
water?

199
00:06:35,115 --> 00:06:36,601
It's hot out there.

200
00:06:36,781 --> 00:06:38,894
Would you like to sit down?

201
00:06:39,243 --> 00:06:41,410
She sat Helen down in the air

202
00:06:41,410 --> 00:06:44,623
conditioning, honey, and brought her a cold

203
00:06:44,623 --> 00:06:47,089
water, and asked her what she was

204
00:06:47,089 --> 00:06:47,986
looking for.

205
00:06:48,166 --> 00:06:49,513
And Helen told her.

206
00:06:49,693 --> 00:06:51,972
About Frank, and the garage,

207
00:06:51,972 --> 00:06:53,356
and the tailgate,

208
00:06:53,356 --> 00:06:55,310
and the sunflower seeds,

209
00:06:55,310 --> 00:06:56,612
and the promise.

210
00:06:56,792 --> 00:06:59,137
And Maria listened to every word.

211
00:06:59,317 --> 00:07:02,011
She didn't look at her watch once.

212
00:07:02,191 --> 00:07:04,267
And when Helen got to the part

213
00:07:04,267 --> 00:07:07,173
about the funeral Caleb couldn't come home

214
00:07:07,173 --> 00:07:09,110
for, Maria's eyes filled up.

215
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:12,340
Maria said, my brother's in the Navy.

216
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:14,981
He missed our dad's funeral too.

217
00:07:15,161 --> 00:07:17,203
And then she said,

218
00:07:17,203 --> 00:07:17,657
Mrs.

219
00:07:17,837 --> 00:07:21,355
Helen, let's find Caleb the right truck.

220
00:07:21,535 --> 00:07:23,683
Not the most expensive one.

221
00:07:23,863 --> 00:07:25,082
The right one.

222
00:07:25,262 --> 00:07:27,393
And she spent two and a half

223
00:07:27,393 --> 00:07:28,535
hours with her,

224
00:07:28,535 --> 00:07:29,372
sweetheart.

225
00:07:29,552 --> 00:07:31,560
Showed her every truck on the lot.

226
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:34,829
Explained everything in plain English.

227
00:07:35,009 --> 00:07:37,011
Took her on a test drive,

228
00:07:37,011 --> 00:07:38,772
with the windows down,

229
00:07:38,772 --> 00:07:41,655
so Helen could feel what Caleb would

230
00:07:41,655 --> 00:07:42,056
feel.

231
00:07:42,405 --> 00:07:44,689
So far, forty years of a red

232
00:07:44,689 --> 00:07:47,299
coffee can, a grandpa's promise,

233
00:07:47,299 --> 00:07:49,175
a salesman who laughed,

234
00:07:49,175 --> 00:07:52,030
and a trainee by the bathroom door.

235
00:07:52,210 --> 00:07:55,084
Helen picked a dark blue pickup,

236
00:07:55,084 --> 00:07:55,623
honey.

237
00:07:55,803 --> 00:07:57,792
Caleb's favorite color,

238
00:07:57,792 --> 00:08:00,645
and a lot like Frank's old truck,

239
00:08:00,645 --> 00:08:01,423
just new.

240
00:08:01,603 --> 00:08:04,593
It came to forty-four thousand eight hundred,

241
00:08:04,593 --> 00:08:05,457
out the door.

242
00:08:05,637 --> 00:08:06,916
And Maria said,

243
00:08:06,916 --> 00:08:09,132
how would you like to pay?

244
00:08:09,312 --> 00:08:11,053
Do you have financing?

245
00:08:11,233 --> 00:08:14,182
And Helen reached into her grocery bag.

246
00:08:14,362 --> 00:08:15,488
Stay with me.

247
00:08:15,838 --> 00:08:17,958
She put that red coffee can on

248
00:08:17,958 --> 00:08:20,360
Maria's desk and took off the lid,

249
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:20,784
honey.

250
00:08:20,964 --> 00:08:23,577
And she started pulling out rolls of

251
00:08:23,577 --> 00:08:25,753
bills, held with rubber bands,

252
00:08:25,753 --> 00:08:27,930
and stacking them on the desk.

253
00:08:28,110 --> 00:08:30,582
Twenties and fifties and hundreds,

254
00:08:30,582 --> 00:08:32,836
forty years of Frank's Fridays.

255
00:08:33,016 --> 00:08:35,349
Maria's mouth fell open.

256
00:08:35,529 --> 00:08:37,379
And across the showroom,

257
00:08:37,379 --> 00:08:39,999
Brad stopped talking on his phone.

258
00:08:40,179 --> 00:08:42,547
And the other salesmen stood up at

259
00:08:42,547 --> 00:08:43,941
their desks to look.

260
00:08:44,290 --> 00:08:47,371
It took the finance manager forty minutes

261
00:08:47,371 --> 00:08:48,574
to count it all,

262
00:08:48,574 --> 00:08:51,129
sweetheart, twice, with a machine.

263
00:08:51,309 --> 00:08:53,293
And while he counted,

264
00:08:53,293 --> 00:08:54,710
Brad came over.

265
00:08:54,890 --> 00:08:56,911
He was all smiles now.

266
00:08:57,091 --> 00:08:58,470
He said, ma'am,

267
00:08:58,470 --> 00:09:01,781
I'm the senior sales associate here.

268
00:09:01,961 --> 00:09:04,016
Maria's still in training.

269
00:09:04,196 --> 00:09:06,431
Let me take care of the paperwork

270
00:09:06,431 --> 00:09:09,072
for you, to make sure everything's done

271
00:09:09,072 --> 00:09:09,479
right.

272
00:09:09,659 --> 00:09:11,479
And he put his hand on the

273
00:09:11,479 --> 00:09:11,969
folder.

274
00:09:12,149 --> 00:09:13,965
He wanted the commission,

275
00:09:13,965 --> 00:09:14,401
honey.

276
00:09:14,581 --> 00:09:16,613
On a sale he'd laughed at.

277
00:09:16,962 --> 00:09:18,721
And Helen took her hand,

278
00:09:18,721 --> 00:09:21,505
her old gardening hand with dirt still

279
00:09:21,505 --> 00:09:22,678
under the nails,

280
00:09:22,678 --> 00:09:24,583
and she put it flat on top

281
00:09:24,583 --> 00:09:25,682
of that folder.

282
00:09:25,862 --> 00:09:26,885
And she said,

283
00:09:26,885 --> 00:09:29,404
young man, when I walked in that

284
00:09:29,404 --> 00:09:32,631
door, I had forty-six thousand dollars in

285
00:09:32,631 --> 00:09:33,733
a grocery bag.

286
00:09:33,913 --> 00:09:36,068
You saw an old woman in dirty

287
00:09:36,068 --> 00:09:36,514
pants.

288
00:09:36,694 --> 00:09:39,364
This young lady saw a person.

289
00:09:39,544 --> 00:09:41,123
She gets every penny.

290
00:09:41,303 --> 00:09:43,583
And the whole showroom heard it,

291
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:46,147
because Helen has always had a voice

292
00:09:46,147 --> 00:09:47,073
that carries.

293
00:09:47,423 --> 00:09:49,785
Brad went red to the tips of

294
00:09:49,785 --> 00:09:51,557
his ears, sweetheart.

295
00:09:51,737 --> 00:09:54,557
He mumbled something and went back to

296
00:09:54,557 --> 00:09:55,243
his desk.

297
00:09:55,423 --> 00:09:57,132
And the general manager,

298
00:09:57,132 --> 00:10:00,052
who'd been watching from his glass office

299
00:10:00,052 --> 00:10:01,120
the whole time,

300
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:03,399
came out and shook Helen's hand.

301
00:10:03,579 --> 00:10:06,091
And then he turned to Maria and

302
00:10:06,091 --> 00:10:07,387
said, nice work.

303
00:10:07,567 --> 00:10:10,194
Come see me in my office after

304
00:10:10,194 --> 00:10:10,632
this.

305
00:10:10,812 --> 00:10:12,704
Maria went white.

306
00:10:12,884 --> 00:10:14,638
She thought she was in trouble.

307
00:10:14,987 --> 00:10:16,584
She wasn't in trouble,

308
00:10:16,584 --> 00:10:17,019
honey.

309
00:10:17,199 --> 00:10:20,237
Helen found out later what Maria hadn't

310
00:10:20,237 --> 00:10:20,938
told her.

311
00:10:21,118 --> 00:10:22,964
It was her last week.

312
00:10:23,144 --> 00:10:25,393
She hadn't sold a single truck in

313
00:10:25,393 --> 00:10:28,051
two months, because the senior men took

314
00:10:28,051 --> 00:10:30,573
every customer who looked like money,

315
00:10:30,573 --> 00:10:32,822
and left her the ones they didn't

316
00:10:32,822 --> 00:10:33,163
want.

317
00:10:33,343 --> 00:10:35,255
She was going to be let go

318
00:10:35,255 --> 00:10:35,990
on Friday.

319
00:10:36,170 --> 00:10:38,713
And she'd been worrying about how to

320
00:10:38,713 --> 00:10:40,408
pay her rent in January.

321
00:10:40,588 --> 00:10:43,204
That commission was more than she'd made

322
00:10:43,204 --> 00:10:43,792
all year.

323
00:10:44,142 --> 00:10:46,464
The manager didn't let her go.

324
00:10:46,644 --> 00:10:48,466
He moved her to the desk by

325
00:10:48,466 --> 00:10:49,477
the front door.

326
00:10:49,657 --> 00:10:51,876
And he called a meeting the next

327
00:10:51,876 --> 00:10:54,510
morning, and he told every salesman in

328
00:10:54,510 --> 00:10:56,451
that building what happened,

329
00:10:56,451 --> 00:10:57,282
and he said,

330
00:10:57,282 --> 00:10:58,114
from now on,

331
00:10:58,114 --> 00:11:00,610
we greet every customer in the first

332
00:11:00,610 --> 00:11:01,441
two minutes.

333
00:11:01,621 --> 00:11:03,235
Every single one.

334
00:11:03,415 --> 00:11:05,760
I don't care what they're wearing.

335
00:11:05,940 --> 00:11:08,975
Helen says Brad lasted about three more

336
00:11:08,975 --> 00:11:11,699
months there, and then he moved on.

337
00:11:12,048 --> 00:11:14,823
Caleb came home on the twenty-second,

338
00:11:14,823 --> 00:11:15,648
sweetheart.

339
00:11:15,828 --> 00:11:17,596
And on Christmas morning,

340
00:11:17,596 --> 00:11:20,143
Helen walked him out to the driveway

341
00:11:20,143 --> 00:11:21,204
in his pajamas,

342
00:11:21,204 --> 00:11:23,609
and there was that dark blue truck

343
00:11:23,609 --> 00:11:25,377
with a big red bow on the

344
00:11:25,377 --> 00:11:25,731
hood.

345
00:11:25,911 --> 00:11:27,701
And on the dashboard,

346
00:11:27,701 --> 00:11:30,599
Helen had put the empty red coffee

347
00:11:30,599 --> 00:11:33,156
can, with Frank's note inside.

348
00:11:33,336 --> 00:11:34,787
Caleb read the note.

349
00:11:34,967 --> 00:11:35,987
And that big,

350
00:11:35,987 --> 00:11:38,969
strong Marine sat down on the tailgate

351
00:11:38,969 --> 00:11:41,166
and cried like a little boy.

352
00:11:41,516 --> 00:11:44,361
And Maria came to Christmas dinner,

353
00:11:44,361 --> 00:11:44,849
honey.

354
00:11:45,029 --> 00:11:46,607
Helen invited her.

355
00:11:46,787 --> 00:11:49,261
Maria brought her mother's tamales,

356
00:11:49,261 --> 00:11:51,452
and Caleb drove them all to the

357
00:11:51,452 --> 00:11:53,997
beach in the new truck that evening,

358
00:11:53,997 --> 00:11:56,259
and they sat on the tailgate and

359
00:11:56,259 --> 00:11:59,227
ate sunflower seeds and watched the trucks

360
00:11:59,227 --> 00:11:59,651
go by.

361
00:11:59,831 --> 00:12:03,762
Maria's the top salesperson at that dealership

362
00:12:03,762 --> 00:12:04,104
now.

363
00:12:04,284 --> 00:12:05,495
And every year,

364
00:12:05,495 --> 00:12:07,837
on the fifteenth of December,

365
00:12:07,837 --> 00:12:09,694
she sends Helen a card.

366
00:12:09,874 --> 00:12:12,475
It says, thank you for seeing me

367
00:12:12,475 --> 00:12:12,800
too.

368
00:12:13,149 --> 00:12:15,726
Here's what I want you to remember,

369
00:12:15,726 --> 00:12:16,168
honey.

370
00:12:16,348 --> 00:12:18,995
Never judge someone by their clothes.

371
00:12:19,175 --> 00:12:21,544
The woman in the dirty garden pants

372
00:12:21,544 --> 00:12:24,048
might be carrying forty years of love

373
00:12:24,048 --> 00:12:25,131
in a coffee can.

374
00:12:25,311 --> 00:12:27,092
Tell me in the comments,

375
00:12:27,092 --> 00:12:30,061
sweetheart, have you ever been judged by

376
00:12:30,061 --> 00:12:31,174
how you looked?

377
00:12:31,354 --> 00:12:33,627
There are more of my family's stories

378
00:12:33,627 --> 00:12:35,777
in the playlist right there on your

379
00:12:35,777 --> 00:12:36,207
screen.

380
00:12:36,387 --> 00:12:37,235
Good night.

381
00:12:37,415 --> 00:12:38,808
Merry Christmas.
